      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have voted for this as it would be nice but there does seem to a bit of an issue with it.\nUsing Z3D for this will likely result in the loss of depth and make the image appear more like you're wearing 3D glasses rather then playing in VR, in this case it wouldn't be too bad as the modes can be switched but just something I thought should be pointed out.\nAlso VRChat itself doesn't have poor optimization, most of the content in this game revolves around user-generated content and most users neglect optimization for their avatar and will have absurd amounts of materials, meshes, bones, etc.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
