      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5bd40a9f7281ea21115a7e5a|full_name}: Yeah, you're right. Stereoscopic effect in Z3D mode will be worse than in G3D. But Z3D isn't GameWarp-mode, where the same image is presented to the right and left eyes and there's no stereoscopic effect at all. When using Z3D, objects on the right and left image will be shifted according to the distance information in the Z-buffer. Stereoscopic effect will be, but not as good as with G3D. However, if the user doesn't have a powerful enough PC, he will prefer to sacrifice the stereoscopic effect to eliminate lags in the game. I would :-) .",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
