  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A 3D-mode switch for VR is required: «Geometry-3D» (G3D) and «Z-Buffer 3D» (Z3D), as implemented in the «vorpX» program. The VRChat-game currently uses G3D-mode. It provides a full-fledged stereoscopic image, but creates a large computational load, since the image is calculated twice: for the right and left eyes. The situation is made worse by the fact that the VRChat has poor optimization. On my PC, for example, in VR-mode, the CPU load is always close to 100%. In Z3D-mode, the scene is calculated only once. After that, using information about the distance to objects stored in the Z-buffer, an image is formed for the right and left eyes. This results in a pseudo-stereoscopic image, but the computational load is twice smaller. With the «G3D / Z3D» switch in the game settings, the users can choose which 3D-mode suits them best for VR, based on the performance of their PC.",
